        "communityKey": "mattagamifn",
        "item": "Mental Health Programming",
        "description": "Previous information: Mattagami FN has a building dedicated to offering services to mental health and wellness support for community members. The services provided include mental health screening and assessments as well as individual, couples, and family counseling. Services include: addiction, depression, family violence, health promotion, stress management. These services and programs are available to members of Mattagami FN who need mental health support as well as those who are in crisis. \n\nPrograms & Services involve: \n\nCommunity Health and Wellness (Mental health supports) \nFamily Well-Being (Supporting families) \nChoose Life (life promotion)\n\nChildren programs\nThe Binoogeesh Centre offers a range of educational programs that are tailored to children. This includes after-school programs, summer camps. The services and programming overall goal is to give children an opportunity to learn, play, and grow in a culturally safe and nurturing environment. \nAddiction services: The Binoogeesh Centre provides essential addiction services. Supports and services include counseling, support groups, and psychoeducation resources for individuals and families who are navigating the complexities of addiction. \n\nReference\n\nhttps://mattagami.com/health/#mental\n\nhttps://mattagami.com/binoogeesh/#choose-life \n\nTribal Nation (Wabun Tribal Council) \n\nCrisis Team Coordination\nWabun Health has supported and been involved with responding to crises in First Nation communities. \n\nReference\n\nhttps://www.wabuntribalcouncil.ca/services/health/ \n\nRevised information: Counseling Services; Psychiatric Consultations; Crisis Intervention; Family Support; Addiction Services; Support Groups; Educational Resources. The Health page lists Counseling Services, Psychiatric Consultations, and Crisis Intervention under Mental Health. The Binoogeesh page says it provides addiction services, including counselling, support groups, and educational resources, and describes Binoogeesh as the place where mental health services are provided.",
