        "description": "Previous information: Health services in Chapleau Cree FN delivery focuses on a holistic approach offering western and traditional healing choices. \n\nServices and programming include: \n\nHealth awareness, education and prevention workshops and seminars, exercise program, doctor available one day per month through Family Health Team\nSupports for older adults and adults with disabilities \nDiabetes Education\nIn-Home and Community Support Services\nProgram facilitator \nRegistered Nurse\nPersonal support worker\nCasual Home support worker\n\nReference\nhttps://chapleaucree.ca/administration/health-centre/ \n\nMushkegowuk Health\n\nPrimary Care services within the Timmins area for Mushkegowuk community members\n\nHealth promotion\nIllness and injury prevention\nDiagnostic tests\nTreatment and management of\nillness and injury\nDiabetes screening\nDiabetes education\nDiabetes foot care services\nCancer screening\nSpecialist referrals\nMinor procedures (wart removal,\ncortisone injections, abscess\ndraining)\nWell-women examinations\nWell-baby/well-child checks\nImmunizations\nPrenatal and postnatal care\nPhysical examinations\nPhlebotomy\nPatient advocacy\nPatient navigation\nOTN services\nRetinal screening\nNon-narcotic medication refills\n\nPatient Advocacy\nPatient Navigator \n\nReference\nhttps://www.mushkegowukhealth.com/_files/ugd/43c8cb_775db8f067d3431eaba8d52c5daf95fb.pdf\n\nRevised Information: The CCHC Health Centre provides health awareness, education and prevention workshops and seminars, an exercise program, and a doctor available one day per month through Family Health Team. It also describes supports for older adults and adults with disabilities to help them remain independent in their own homes as long as possible.",
