    "contact": "Administrative Office: (705) 759-0914\nCommunity Liaison: Linda Robinson - communityliaison@batchewana.ca (705) 989-6019\nCommunications Manager: Alexandra Syrette - alex@batchewana.ca (705) 759-0914 ext. 247",
    "physical": "The Community Health Team offers public health programs and supports, including immunizations, communicable-disease prevention, chronic disease screening/management, health-system navigation, referrals, healthy child development supports, environmental health, and traditional health programming. The Home and Community Care Program provides homemaking, personal support work, respite, and community-support referrals, and Medical Transportation supports access to appointments including doctors, dentists, specialists, therapy, and traditional healers.",
    "mental": "The Community Wellness Team provides voluntary mental health and substance-use supports for members aged 12+, including Adult Wellness, Youth Wellness, Counselling, and NNADAP / Outreach / Aftercare. Publicly listed activities include counselling and psychotherapy, addiction support, harm reduction, psychoeducation, referrals, and group programming. These help fill gaps in counselling, substance-use support, prevention, and follow-up care",
    "spiritual": "Publicly listed traditional health programming, including name, colour and clan ceremonies, and medical transportation can support appointments with a traditional healer.",
    "emotional": "Through the Community Wellness Team and Family Wellness Team. Support including supportive counselling, phychoeducation, family advocacy, in-home support, caregiver support through Grandmas and Aunties, and community wellness programming.",
    "survivors": "Supported through community wellness and mental wellness support, and the community has publicly hosted gathering invloving survivors and intergenerational family members.\nExternal advocay/support may also exist through AIAI.",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through the Youth Centre, Youth Wellness, Education/Learning services, and post-secondary support, including guidance, career counselling, and post-secondary funding administration.\nProgram & Services",
    "connect": "Recreation Activator programminh includes childern, youth, adults, and Elders, and offers community-wide cultural, land-based, and recreational aactivities that could support intergenerational connection.\nRecreation Activator",
