    "name": "Wahnapitae First Nation",
    "section": "Algoma District First Nation Communities",
    "link": "https://wahnapitaefirstnation.com/",
    "contact": "Beatrice Debassige - Health Assistant\nPhone: 705-858-7700\nEmail: beatrice.debassige@wahnapitaefn.com\n\nTaylor Bertrim - Governance & Research Specialist\nPhone: (705) 858-0610 | Ext. 253\nEmail: taylor.bertrim@wahnapitaefn.com\n\nMarilyn Nicholls - Director of Education Departmentc\nPhone: 705-858-0610 | Ext. 209\nEmail: marilyn.nicholls@wahnapitaefn.com\n\nContact page",
    "physical": "The community offers health services and programs through the Norman Recollet Health Services Centre, including Aboriginal Diabetes Initiative, Healthy Babies, Healthy Children, Building Healthy Communities, Healthy Child Development, Canada Prenatal Nutrition Program, Home and Community Care, massage therapy, medical transportation, dental information and products, and community support services.",
    "mental": "The community offers Mental Wellness/Land Base and Community Wellness Worker support through the Norman Recollet Health Services Centre.",
    "spiritual": "The community offers Mental Wellness/Land Base through the Norman Recollet Health Services Centre. The community also shares traditional teachings, ceremonies, and land-based cultural activities through newsletters and related materials, including a Traditional teaching event and land-based worker role centered on traditional teachings, life skills, traditional activities, and ceremonies.",
    "emotional": "Building Healthy Communities, Home and Community Care, Community Support Services, Family Well Being",
    "survivors": "The community offers broader wellness, cultural, and gathering supports through Mental Wellness/Land Base, land-based teachings, and Elders-focused community gatherings.",
    "youth": "The community offers youth support through Grade School Support, Adult Education, and Post-Secondary education services. The Post-Secondary page says the policy was created to encourage registered band members to acquire post-secondary qualifications and provide funding equitably. Community newsletters also show After School and Youth Leadership Program activities, including partnerships that provide safe, meaningful, and supervised activities for youth, and regular youth programming for children and teens",
    "connect": "The community offers intergenerational and land-based gathering spaces through the Reclaiming Our Knowledge: Elders & Local Knowledge Gathering, where Elders and youth shared stories about their relationship to the land. Community newsletters also show youth leadership and afterschool spaces.",
