        "description": "Previous information:\nthey support their youth through education and support from the community through recreational events https://oneida.on.ca/education/\n\nRevised information:\nOneida Nation of the Thames supports youth through the Education Office, Head Start Family Resource Program, Child Care Center, Oneida Language & Cultural Centre, Standing Stone School, Employment & Training, Youth Prevention Program, and community events/programs such as Two-Spirit Youth Circle, Youth Cooking Nights, Traditional Knowledge and Wellness – Youth, Family Yoga, family skating, lacrosse drop-in, and language learning activities. The Education Department supports members in achieving academic goals through quality educational programs and services, while Employment & Training helps Oneida members improve skills and find employment. These supports help youth through early learning, school support, language and cultural learning, wellness/prevention, recreation, food skills, employment readiness, and community connection.",
