    "name": "Wahta Mohawk",
    "section": "South",
    "link": "https://wahtamohawks.com",
    "contact": "Administration\nLisa Tabobondung - Senior Administrator\nPhone: 705-762-2354 | Ext. 231\nEmail: lisa.tabobondung@wahtamohawks.ca\n\nNicole Holmes - Executive Assistant & Receptionist\nPhone: 705-762-2354 | Ext. 225\nEmail: nicole.holmes@wahtamohawks.ca\n\nChristine Cox - Health & Social Services Director        \nchristine.cox@wahtamohawks.ca\nPhone: 705-762-2354 | Ext. 273\n\nCarol Holmes - Education Services Manager\nPhone: 705-762-2354 | Ext. 233\ncarol.holmes@wahtamohawks.ca\n\nMaintenance & Public Works\nHarry Byrne -\tMaintenance Supervisor\nPhone: 705-641-0833\nEmail: harry.byrne@wahtamohawks.ca\n\nEvan Holmes - Public Works\t\nPhone: 705-644-9884\nEmail: evan.holmes@wahtamohawks.ca\n\nContact Us",
    "physical": "Wahta Mohawks offers physical health supports through Health & Social Services, including Diabetes Support, Seniors Services, Homemakers/PSW Services, Non-Insured Health Benefits, and Medical Transportation. The Seniors Services program supports the physical, mental, and spiritual health of members and provides case management, health-care education, equipment loans such as walkers/wheelchairs/crutches, homemaking, PSW supports, Meals on Wheels, home visits, home safety, mobility support, Lifeline emergency response, and a Bala Taxi partnership for medical transportation needs. Diabetes programming includes diabetes education, prevention, management, workshops, support groups, resources, and Meals on Wheels support for seniors. Social Services also oversees Non-Insured Health Benefits and Medical Transportation. These services help fill gaps in diabetes support, seniors’ health, home care, mobility/accessibility, medical transportation, health education, emergency response, meals, and support for aging members to remain safely at home.",
    "mental": "Wahta Mohawks offers mental health programming through Health & Social Services, including Mental Health and Addictions support, crisis support, counselling referrals, health promotion, and community wellness supports. The Health & Social Services area connects members to programs that support overall wellness, while Social Services provides support and referrals for members who need help accessing services. These supports help fill gaps in mental health access, addictions support, crisis response, referrals, service navigation, and community wellness.",
    "spiritual": "Wahta Mohawks supports spiritual/cultural wellbeing through Education programming that engages the community in Mohawk history, culture, traditions, and language preservation, and through wholistic and culturally driven programming. The Education page says its goals are to engage the community in Mohawk history, culture, traditions and language preservation and to cultivate safe, vibrant and engaged families and community through wholistic and culturally driven programming. Wahta also supports learning through language camp programming focused on experiential language learning, games, discussions, storytelling, and land-based learning experiences. The Language Instructor/Camp Facilitator posting says the program supports participants in strengthening their connection to culture and language through daily programming. These supports help fill gaps in cultural connection, Mohawk language preservation, traditional learning, land-based learning, family/community connection, and wholistic culturally driven support.",
    "emotional": "Wahta Mohawks supports emotional wellbeing through Social Services, Child & Family Services, Seniors Services, and community wellness supports. Social Services provides referrals and assistance for members accessing services, Child & Family Services supports children, youth, and families, and Seniors Services provides home visits, case management, health-care education, homemaking/PSW supports, Meals on Wheels, mobility support, home safety support, and Lifeline emergency response. These supports help fill gaps in family support, service navigation, social support, Elder support, safety, home-based support, and emotional wellbeing connected to daily living needs.",
    "survivors": "Wahta Mohawks supports Survivors through Seniors Services, Social Services, Child & Family Services, and Education programming. Seniors Services provides case management, home visits, health-care education, equipment loans, homemaking/PSW supports, Meals on Wheels, mobility support, home safety support, Lifeline emergency response, and transportation support through the Bala Taxi partnership. Social Services and Child & Family Services provide referrals, assistance, and family support, while Education programming supports Mohawk history, culture, traditions, language preservation, and wholistic culturally driven programming. These supports help Survivors through home-based care, meals, safety support, mobility support, transportation, service navigation, family support, and cultural/language connection.",
    "youth": "Wahta Mohawks supports youth through Child & Family Services, Education, Employment & Training, Social Services, and language/culture programming. Child & Family Services supports children, youth, and families, while Education programming supports Mohawk history, culture, traditions, language preservation, and wholistic culturally driven programming. Employment & Training supports members with education, training, and employment pathways, and Social Services provides referrals and assistance for members accessing services. Wahta also supports youth connection to culture and language through language camp programming focused on experiential language learning, games, discussions, storytelling, and land-based learning experiences.",
    "connect": "Wahta Mohawks can connect Survivors and youth through Education programming, language/culture learning, Child & Family Services, and Seniors Services. Education supports Mohawk history, culture, traditions, language preservation, and wholistic culturally driven programming, while language camp programming supports experiential language learning, games, discussions, storytelling, and land-based learning experiences. Seniors Services and Child & Family Services can support intergenerational connection through Elder support, youth/family support, cultural learning, storytelling, and community-based activities.",
