    "contact": "Main contact: PO Box 146, Pipestone, MB R0M 1T0\nPhone: 204 854 2959\nFax: 204 854 2525\nHealth Office phone: 204 854 2990\n\nSources:\n1- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/contact-us/\n2- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/administration-2/\n3- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/services/health-services/\n4- https://fnp-ppn.aadnc-aandc.gc.ca/fnp/Main/Search/FNMain.aspx?BAND_NUMBER=289&lang=eng\n5- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/services/",
    "physical": "The Health Services Centre provides community health programs and open Health Office access. Home and Community Care with a Community Health Nurse, Community Health Resource and Aboriginal Diabetes Initiative, and the Canadian Prenatal Nutrition Program. Telehealth is available through the Canupawakpa Health Centre.\nSources:\n\n1- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/services/health-services/\n2- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/administration-2/\n3- https://mbtelehealth.ca/locations/first-nations/",
    "mental": "Missing information",
    "spiritual": "Medicine picking with Elders, traditional knowledge sharing, language, and youth Elder activities are described through Southern Chiefs Organization coverage of Canupawakpa wellness and youth gathering activities. Land Base Culture is associated with the community Jordan’s Principle programming.\nSources:\n1- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/building-health-and-wellness-in-canupawakpawe-would-now-like-you-to-meet-tate-po/871121821709871/\n2- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/administration-2/",
    "emotional": "Missing information",
    "survivors": "Missing information",
    "youth": "A three day land based Youth Gathering for ages 15 to 30 included cooking classes, hikes, medicine picking with Elders, traditional knowledge sharing, language, and youth Elder connection. Also, Jordan’s Principle Child First, the Brighter Futures Initiative, and the Wambdi Iyotaka Nursery and Kindergarten School are listed on the community services and administration pages.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/building-health-and-wellness-in-canupawakpawe-would-now-like-you-to-meet-tate-po/871121821709871/\n2- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/services/\n3- https://canupawakpanation.com/index.php/administration-2/",
