    "contact": "Band office: Box 240, Island Lake, SK S0M 3G0\nPhone: 306 837 2188\nFax: 306 837 2266\nYouth Centre phone: 306 837 9644\nHealth Centre phone: 306 837 2265\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.mltc.net/nations/mlcn/\n2- https://www.mltc.net/ministikwan-lake-cree-nation-opens-youth-prevention-centre/\n3- https://islandlakehc.net/\n4- https://www.mltc.net/services/",
    "physical": "Island Lake Health Centre states it provides medical services including diagnostics, treatment, surgery, vaccine, and emergency services.\nMLTC Health and Social Development provides community health support and clinical or program support across MLTC First Nations.\nCommunity health services are also delivered in partnership with the Northern Inter Tribal Health Authority.\n\nSources:\n1- https://islandlakehc.net/\n2- https://www.mltc.net/services/",
    "mental": "The Ministikwan Lake Youth and Prevention Centre offers one to one support, with community Elders available for one to one talks to help with addictions. The source also identifies prevention workers serving youth and families.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.mltc.net/ministikwan-lake-cree-nation-opens-youth-prevention-centre/",
    "spiritual": "The Ministikwan Lake Youth and Prevention Centre involves community Elders in parenting classes, oral tradition storytelling, one to one talks, and traditional teachings used to address contemporary challenges.\nSources:\n1- https://www.mltc.net/ministikwan-lake-cree-nation-opens-youth-prevention-centre/",
    "emotional": "The Youth and Prevention Centre conducts weekly home visits and safety checks. It provides prevention support, including help with clothing and food in dire situations, for community youth and families.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.mltc.net/ministikwan-lake-cree-nation-opens-youth-prevention-centre/",
    "survivors": "Missing information",
    "youth": "The Ministikwan Lake Youth and Prevention Centre was developed to keep community youth safe and fed through weekly home visits and safety checks.\nThe centre includes a full gym and a pool table.\nMLTC also delivers Child and Family Services and Jordan’s Principle to Ministikwan.\nSources:\n1- https://www.mltc.net/ministikwan-lake-cree-nation-opens-youth-prevention-centre/\n2- https://www.mltc.net/service/family-services/",
