        "description": "Previous information:\npopulation gathered from Government of Canada as of October 2025\nregistered population - 7207\nRegistered Population - Government of Canada  \n\npopulation information from Wikipedia source as of 2019\ntotal population - 6475\nOnion Lake Cree Nation - Wikipedia\n\nadditional information from The Gladue Rights Research Database.\npopulation - 6782\nOnion Lake Cree Nation | Gladue Rights Research Database\n\nRevised information:\n2024 registered population split: 4,537 on reserve and on Crown land, 2,566 off reserve.\nOnion Lake Cree Nation is a Plains Cree Treaty 6 First Nation.\nReserve land is 57,737.5 ha and is located 50 km north of Lloydminster.\nIt is Canada’s only Cree Nation straddling the Saskatchewan Alberta border, with reserves including Seekaskootch 119 and Makaoo 120.\nSources:\n1- https://www.sac-isc.gc.ca/eng/1753213597358/1753213649039\n2- https://onionlake.ca/leadership/\n3- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onion_Lake_Cree_Nation",
