    "name": "Peguis First Nation",
    "section": "West",
    "link": "https://peguis.ca/",
    "contact": "First Nation profile: PO Box 10, Peguis Reserve, MB R0C 3J0\nBand phone: 204 645 2359\nFax: 204 645 2360\nPeguis Health Centre phone: 204 645 2169\nPeguis Health Centre hours: Monday to Friday, 9:30 AM to 4:30 PM\nPeguis Al Care Treatment Centre phone: 204 645 2666\nPeguis CFS Peguis office phone: 204 645 2049\nPeguis CFS toll free: 1 877 777 2049\n\nSources:\n1- https://fnp-ppn.aadnc-aandc.gc.ca/fnp/Main/Search/FNMain.aspx?BAND_NUMBER=269&lang=eng\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/peguis-health-centre\n3- https://www.peguiscfs.ca/reports\n4- https://mbtelehealth.ca/locations/first-nations/\n5- https://peguis.ca/",
    "physical": "Peguis Health Centre operates departments including Home and Community Care, Long Term Care, Community Health, and Community Wellness.\nServices include prevention, screening, treatment, and case management.\nThe Health Centre page lists Non Insured Health Benefits accommodations, meals, medical transportation benefits, health board information, and Peguis Health Centre contact details.\nSeasonal flu vaccination is offered at Peguis Health Centre with Nurse on Call.\nPeguis Senior Centre provides Elder care including spiritual, physical, and emotional support.\n\nSources:\n1- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/peguis-health-centre\n2- https://peguis.ca/\n3- https://eolfn.lakeheadu.ca/the-communities/peguis-first-nation",
    "mental": "Peguis Al Care Treatment Centre is NNADAP funded and provides culturally anchored addiction recovery for adults 18 and older through residential and outpatient programs on a 42 day cycle. Services include intake assessment, alcohol and drug education, relapse prevention education, crisis intervention, case management, group and individual counselling, referrals, life skills, and recreation therapy.\nPeguis also has a Wellness Team department.\n\nSources:\n1- https://mb.211.ca/detail/97561570/\n2- https://www.drugrehab.ca/directory/item/peguis-al-care-treatment-centre.html\n3- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/peguis-al-care-treatment-centre",
    "spiritual": "Spiritual and cultural care is provided through traditional healing resources such as Matootoo Lake Lodge and Elder spiritual care at Peguis Senior Centre. The Al Care Treatment Centre incorporates culturally informed activities as part of treatment.\n\nSources:\n1- https://mb.211.ca/detail/97561570/\n2- https://eolfn.lakeheadu.ca/the-communities/peguis-first-nation\n3- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/peguis-al-care-treatment-centre",
    "emotional": "The Al Care Treatment Centre provides group and individual counselling, crisis intervention, treatment planning, referral, life skills, and personal development. Peguis Child and Family Services states its mission is to provide child and family services to Peguis members who request services wherever they reside in Canada.\n\nSources:\n1- https://mb.211.ca/detail/97561570/\n2- https://www.peguiscfs.ca/\n3- https://www.drugrehab.ca/directory/item/peguis-al-care-treatment-centre.html",
    "survivors": "A Honouring Survivors message from Southern Chiefs Organization indicates Peguis dedicated the last week of September to Elders and the community’s Indian Residential School and Day School survivors.\nPeguis also posted a Federal Indian Day School Settlement notice for claimants.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/honouring-survivors-peguis-first-nation-dedicated-the-last-week-of-september-to-/467626572059400/\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/communications/notices/federal-indian-day-school-settlement",
    "youth": "Peguis Child and Family Services provides child and family services to Peguis members wherever they reside in Canada. The Peguis School Board and Post Secondary Department serve students. Al Care is an adults only program.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.peguiscfs.ca/\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/membership",
    "connect": "survivor honouring activities and Peguis CFS youth and family services.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/honouring-survivors-peguis-first-nation-dedicated-the-last-week-of-september-to-/467626572059400/\n2- https://www.peguiscfs.ca/",
    "population": "12051.0",
    "populationNote": "2024 registered population split: 3,882 on reserve and on Crown land, 8,169 off reserve.\nPeguis is a Treaty 1 First Nation in Manitoba with Ojibway Saulteaux and Cree members.\nThe main reserve is Peguis 1B, roughly 190 km north of Winnipeg.\nPeguis is a member of the Interlake Reserves Tribal Council and is named for Chief Peguis.\nSources:\n1- https://www.sac-isc.gc.ca/eng/1753213597358/1753213649039\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/about\n3- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peguis_First_Nation",
    "additionalLinks": "Official Peguis site\nPeguis Health Centre\nPeguis CFS reports\nStrategic Planning Sessions page\nSurvivor honouring post\nGovernment profile\nPeguis consolidated financial statements page\nSources:\n1- https://peguis.ca/\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/peguis-health-centre\n3- https://www.peguiscfs.ca/reports\n4- https://peguis.ca/index.php/events/events-past/strategic-planning-sessions\n5- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/honouring-survivors-peguis-first-nation-dedicated-the-last-week-of-september-to-/467626572059400/\n6- https://fnp-ppn.aadnc-aandc.gc.ca/fnp/Main/Search/FNMain.aspx?BAND_NUMBER=269&lang=eng\n7- https://peguis.ca/index.php/departments/band-office/finance/peguis-first-nation-consolidated-financial-statements",
