        "community": "Peguis First Nation",
        "communityKey": "peguisfn",
        "item": "How are survivors supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nResidential School Support Services: A specific program is offered to address the needs of members who have been impacted by the legacy of residential schooling.\nTraditional Elder Services | Peguis CFS\n\nRevised information:\nA Honouring Survivors message from Southern Chiefs Organization indicates Peguis dedicated the last week of September to Elders and the community’s Indian Residential School and Day School survivors.\nPeguis also posted a Federal Indian Day School Settlement notice for claimants.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.facebook.com/SCOIncMB/posts/honouring-survivors-peguis-first-nation-dedicated-the-last-week-of-september-to-/467626572059400/\n2- https://peguis.ca/index.php/communications/notices/federal-indian-day-school-settlement",
