    "link": "https://svdngovernance.com/",
    "contact": "SVDN contact page: PO Box 38, Griswold, MB R0M 0S0\nBand administration phone: 204 855 2671\nToll free: 1 866 721 0293\nContact page fax: 204 855 2544\nFirst Nation Profile fax: 204 855 2436\nSioux Valley Health Centre phone: 204 855 2690\nSioux Valley Health Centre fax: 204 855 2833\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/contact-us/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n3- https://ccmbindigenouscommunityprofiles.ca/community/sioux-valley-dakota-nation/\n4- https://fnp-ppn.aadnc-aandc.gc.ca/fnp/Main/Search/FNMain.aspx?BAND_NUMBER=290&lang=eng",
    "physical": "Sioux Valley Health Centre lists Aboriginal Diabetes Initiative, Canada Prenatal Nutrition Program, Community Health Nursing, Immunizations, Chronic Conditions, Healthy Babies, Foot Care, Home and Community Care, and Medical Transportation.\nThe Health Centre hosts visiting physicians, dieticians, nurse practitioners, and full time dental therapy services.\nThe Health Centre has achieved first level Accreditation Canada status and recently consolidated health and wellness programs under one roof after a major renovation.\nSioux Valley Dakota Oyate Lodge has provided personal and long term care since 1983.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/svdn-health-centre/\n3- https://svdngovernance.com/programs/",
    "mental": "Sioux Valley Health Centre lists Community Wellness, Mental Health, Addictions Services, and Prevention Program. The 2024 to 2025 Annual Report mentions AA, mental health appointments and drop ins, traditional healing strategies, and youth mental health and addictions prevention services.\nSecond level mental wellness services, including crisis response, counselling, and community wellness, are available through Dakota Ojibway Health Services.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/wp-content/uploads/SVDN-2024-2025-Annual-Report.pdf\n3- https://svdngovernance.com/governance-news/svdn-2024-2025-annual-report/\n4- https://www.dotc.mb.ca/dotc-health-services",
    "spiritual": "The 2024 to 2025 Annual Report mentions traditional healing strategies. The IRS Survivors: Voices and Memories initiative honours the residential school stories of SVDN members in a community book and exhibit.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/wp-content/uploads/SVDN-2024-2025-Annual-Report.pdf\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/recent-news/svdn-irs-survivors-voices-and-memories-2026-04-23-2026-05-07/",
    "emotional": "Sioux Valley Health Centre lists Community Wellness, Mental Health, Addictions Services, Prevention Program, Youth Activities, and Brighter Futures. IRS Survivors: Voices and Memories gathers and honours the stories of SVDN members who attended residential schools. SVDN’s Residential School Missing Children’s Investigation focuses on helping families through loss and trauma.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/recent-news/svdn-irs-survivors-voices-and-memories-2026-04-23-2026-05-07/\n3- https://amp.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/brandon-residential-school-sioux-valley-1.6768456",
    "survivors": "SVDN supports survivors through its Residential School Missing Children’s Investigation connected to Brandon Indian Residential School, using forensic methods, archival research, and interviews with survivors. The IRS Survivors: Voices and Memories community book and exhibit honours members who attended residential schools. A councillor holds the Nation’s Indian Residential Schools portfolio.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/recent-news/svdn-irs-survivors-voices-and-memories-2026-04-23-2026-05-07/\n2- https://amp.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/brandon-residential-school-sioux-valley-1.6768456",
    "youth": "Sioux Valley Health Centre lists Youth Activities and Brighter Futures. The 2024 to 2025 Annual Report mentions youth mental health and addictions prevention services. SVDN Jordan’s Principle provides additional support services to on reserve children and youth ages 0 to 21, plus parents and siblings. Sioux Valley Schools, from Headstart to Grade 12, and the School Board serve students.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/wp-content/uploads/SVDN-2024-2025-Annual-Report.pdf\n3- https://svdngovernance.com/programs/svdn-health/\n4- https://svdngovernance.com/",
