        "communityKey": "siouxvalleydakotanation",
        "item": "Physical Health Programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nPrograms like Brighter Futures and the Canada Prenatal Nutrition Program are designed to support the health and well-being of youth and families. \n\n-Sioux Valley Health Center provides health services to members of the community, and hosts visiting physicians, dieticians, nurse practitioners and full-time dental therapy services on a regular basis. \nSVDN Health Centre – Sioux Valley Dakota Nation\n\nhttps://cysticfibrosis.ca/mental-health/stanton-indigenous-wellness-program\n\n\nRevised information:\nSioux Valley Health Centre lists Aboriginal Diabetes Initiative, Canada Prenatal Nutrition Program, Community Health Nursing, Immunizations, Chronic Conditions, Healthy Babies, Foot Care, Home and Community Care, and Medical Transportation.\nThe Health Centre hosts visiting physicians, dieticians, nurse practitioners, and full time dental therapy services.\nThe Health Centre has achieved first level Accreditation Canada status and recently consolidated health and wellness programs under one roof after a major renovation.\nSioux Valley Dakota Oyate Lodge has provided personal and long term care since 1983.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/svdn-health-centre/\n3- https://svdngovernance.com/programs/",
