        "item": "Mental Health Programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nSVDN Health Centre – Sioux Valley Dakota Nation\n\n The SVDN Health Centre has undergone renovations to bring various health and wellness programs, including mental health and addictions services, under one roof, improving coordination of care and accessibility for community members.\n\nRevised information:\nSioux Valley Health Centre lists Community Wellness, Mental Health, Addictions Services, and Prevention Program. The 2024 to 2025 Annual Report mentions AA, mental health appointments and drop ins, traditional healing strategies, and youth mental health and addictions prevention services.\nSecond level mental wellness services, including crisis response, counselling, and community wellness, are available through Dakota Ojibway Health Services.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/uncategorized/svdn-health/\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/wp-content/uploads/SVDN-2024-2025-Annual-Report.pdf\n3- https://svdngovernance.com/governance-news/svdn-2024-2025-annual-report/\n4- https://www.dotc.mb.ca/dotc-health-services",
