        "item": "Spiritual support programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\n-Spiritual support is embedded within community programs. For example, the Sioux Valley Gaming Centre uses its profits to support community and spiritual gatherings, including the annual Pow Wow and Dakota Nation Winterfest.\n\n- The Gaming Centre provides direct assistance to elders where no other funding is available and supports youth sports and recreation fees, reinforcing community values of sharing and helping each other.\nSVDN Gaming Centre – Sioux Valley Dakota Nation\n\nRevised information:\nThe 2024 to 2025 Annual Report mentions traditional healing strategies. The IRS Survivors: Voices and Memories initiative honours the residential school stories of SVDN members in a community book and exhibit.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/wp-content/uploads/SVDN-2024-2025-Annual-Report.pdf\n2- https://svdngovernance.com/recent-news/svdn-irs-survivors-voices-and-memories-2026-04-23-2026-05-07/",
