        "item": "How are survivors supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\n- Events are held for survivors and families to share their stories and process trauma related to residential schools. The community has supported initiatives to identify unmarked graves at the Brandon Indian Residential School, providing a space for grief and closure.\nBrandon Indian Residential School Cemeteries Project – Sioux Valley Dakota Nation \n\n- Cultural revitalization: The nation is working on revitalizing Dakota culture and language and incorporating them into its programs and services\n\n\nRevised information:\nSVDN supports survivors through its Residential School Missing Children’s Investigation connected to Brandon Indian Residential School, using forensic methods, archival research, and interviews with survivors. The IRS Survivors: Voices and Memories community book and exhibit honours members who attended residential schools. A councillor holds the Nation’s Indian Residential Schools portfolio.\n\nSources:\n1- https://svdngovernance.com/recent-news/svdn-irs-survivors-voices-and-memories-2026-04-23-2026-05-07/\n2- https://amp.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/brandon-residential-school-sioux-valley-1.6768456",
