    "name": "York Factory First Nation",
    "section": "West",
    "link": "http://www.yffn.ca/",
    "contact": "York Factory First Nation: General Delivery, York Landing, MB R0B 2B0\nPhone: 204 341 2180\nFuture Development phone: 204 341 2236\nChief and Council fax: 204 341 2322\nMember of Keewatin Tribal Council\nKTC sub office: 23 Nickel Road, Thompson, MB\nKTC phone: 204 677 2341\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.yffn.ca/\n2- https://www.gov.mb.ca/inr/publications/pubs/indigenous-organizations-in-manitoba.pdf\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/york-factory-first-nation\n4- http://www.yffn.ca/kawechiwasik/chief-council/",
    "physical": "Health services are delivered through the Keewatin Tribal Council Health Department.\nKTC Health Department lists Nursing and Referral or Medical Transportation teams and services including Home and Community Care, Maternal Child Health, Foot Care, Aboriginal Diabetes Initiative, and Medical Transportation.\nThe KTC 2023 to 2024 Health annual report also identifies these Nursing and Referral or Medical Transportation services.\nYork Factory’s own website lists community programs and services.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.ktc.ca/health\n2- https://www.ktc.ca/\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/wcm-docs/docs/programs_and_services/ktc_health_annual_report_2023_24.pdf",
    "mental": "The KTC Mental Wellness Team provides crisis response, Brighter Futures and Building Healthy Communities, NNADAP, National Aboriginal Youth Suicide Prevention Program coordination, and culturally sensitive wellness services to KTC communities. The York Factory Prevention Centre project includes therapy rooms and wellness or recreational spaces.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.ktc.ca/health\n2- https://iaac-aeic.gc.ca/050/evaluations/proj/86120?culture=en-CA\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/mental-wellness-team\n4- https://www.ktc.ca/wcm-docs/docs/programs_and_services/ktc_health_annual_report_2023_24.pdf",
    "spiritual": "The KTC Indian Residential Schools program lists community based cultural supports, cultural events and ceremonies, gatherings, and workshops for KTC communities.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.ktc.ca/indian-residential-schools",
    "emotional": "The KTC Indian Residential Schools program lists cultural and emotional supports for KTC communities. The KTC Mental Wellness Team provides crisis response and wellness services. The York Factory Prevention Centre project description includes therapy rooms and wellness spaces for a First Nation Child and Family Services prevention centre.\n\nSources:\n1- https://iaac-aeic.gc.ca/050/evaluations/proj/86120?culture=en-CA\n2- https://www.ktc.ca/indian-residential-schools\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/mental-wellness-team",
    "survivors": "Missing information",
    "youth": "KTC Jordan’s Principle community based initiatives provide services, supports, and resources for children and families. KTC’s Health annual report references youth workers under Jordan’s Principle. KTC health services include National Aboriginal Youth Suicide Prevention Strategy among KTC services. A new York Factory First Nation Child and Family Services prevention centre is is described as including gym or community space, therapy rooms, and wellness or recreational spaces.\n\nSources:\n1- https://www.ktc.ca/\n2- https://iaac-aeic.gc.ca/050/evaluations/proj/86120?culture=en-CA\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/jordans-principle-initiative",
    "connect": "Missing information",
    "population": "1669.0",
    "populationNote": "2024 registered population split: 455 on reserve and on Crown land, 1,214 off reserve.\nYork Factory First Nation is a Swampy Cree Treaty 5 community in northern Manitoba.\nThe main reserve is York Landing, also called Kawechiwasik, on the east bank of the Nelson River about 116 km from Thompson.\nThe community’s Cree people originate from York Factory on Hudson Bay and relocated to York Landing after the Hudson’s Bay Company post closed in 1957.\nAffiliations include Keewatin Tribal Council, Manitoba Keewatinowi Okimakanak, and the Assembly of Manitoba Chiefs.\nSources:\n1- https://www.sac-isc.gc.ca/eng/1753213597358/1753213649039\n2- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Factory_First_Nation\n3- https://www.ktc.ca/york-factory-first-nation",
