    "name": "Cockburn Island / Zhiibaahaasing First Nation",
    "section": "North",
    "link": "Community does not have a dedicated standalone website",
    "contact": "Main Phone: (705) 283-3963 (also Health/Econ Dev)\nFax: (705) 283-3964\nEmail (Band Office): zhiiband@manitoulin.net\nPhysical Address: 36 Sagon Rd, Zhiibaahaasing, ON P0P 1Y0\nMailing Address: P.O. Box 1, Zhiibaahaasing, ON P0P 1X0",
    "physical": "Physical health support is listed through the Zhiibaahaasing Health Clinic, which provides programs and services that promote physical and mental health for community members. The Health Services record lists coordination with visiting doctors and nurse practitioners, health awareness/education/prevention workshops, clinics such as diabetes, immunization, sexual health and communicable diseases, foot-care sessions, intake, referrals, advocacy, prenatal care coordination, and home visits for the sick, elderly, new mothers, and people with health-care needs. The Zhiibaahaasing Health Clinic site record also lists related programs including Diabetes Program, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, Home and Community Care Program, and NNADAP.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is listed through Zhiibaahaasing Health Services and related community programs. The Health Services record states that the Health Clinic provides programs promoting physical and mental health and addresses individual health-care needs through intake, referrals, advocacy, and coordination with health professionals. The public agency profile also lists National Native Alcohol and Drug Abuse Program and Family Well Being Program as Zhiibaahaasing programs, while the Family Well Being Program record includes counselling, child/youth support groups, alcohol and drug abuse prevention/intervention, referrals, school programs, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "spiritual": "A specific standalone spiritual-support program was not clearly found in the public Zhiibaahaasing records. Howerever, broader cultural/spiritual support can be reflected through the Family Well Being Program, which lists traditional land-based healing events, community feasts, activities that revitalize Native language, family circles, counselling, and child/youth support groups. This should be recorded as broader cultural and land-based support, not as a confirmed separate spiritual-support department.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through Zhiibaahaasing’s broader health, family wellbeing, and addictions-related programs. The Health Services record lists intake, referrals, advocacy, health education, and coordination with health professionals, while the Family Well Being Program lists family circles, counselling, child/youth support groups, referrals, alcohol and drug abuse prevention/intervention, school programs, traditional land-based healing events, and community events such as feasts. These supports help address emotional wellness, family stress, prevention, addictions, and connection to culturally grounded support.",
    "survivors": "No specific Survivor support program was clearly found. Howerever, broader support can be provided through the community’s listed Health Services, Family Well Being Program, Home and Community Care Program, and related wellness supports. The Family Well Being Program includes family circles, counselling, child/youth support groups, traditional land-based healing events, community feasts, language-revitalization activities, and referrals.",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Zhiibaahaasing’s listed Family Well Being Program, Healthy Families, and health-related services. The Family Well Being Program includes activities that revitalize Native language, alcohol and drug abuse prevention/intervention, community events such as feasts, family circles, counselling, child/youth support groups, referrals to other programs and services, school programs, and traditional land-based healing events. The Health Clinic site record also lists Healthy Babies Healthy Children and other health programs connected to children, families, and community wellness.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through existing community pathways listed under the Family Well Being Program, especially family circles, child/youth support groups, school programs, language-revitalization activities, traditional land-based healing events, and community feasts. These activities create possible spaces for Elders/knowledge holders and youth to connect around culture, language, family wellbeing, and land-based healing.",
