        "communityKey": "constancelakefn",
        "item": "How are youth supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\n Programs at Mamawmatawa Holistic Education Centre, Junior Canadian Rangers (First Aid, safe rifle use, traditions), and employment resources.\n\n\nKunuwanimano Child & Family Services offers intake, case management, cultural care, and family support. \nKunuwanimano Child and Family Services\n\nRevised information:\nConstance Lake First Nation supports youth through Choose Life, Jordan’s Principle, Social and Wellness, Education, language/culture programming, and youth portfolio leadership. Choose Life promotes mental health awareness, suicide prevention, and community wellness through culturally appropriate programs, counselling services, and peer-support initiatives. Jordan’s Principle is described as ensuring community children receive equitable access to government services, healthcare, education, and support without service delays or denials. The Culture and Language page says youth are eager to learn, and that CLFN supports language immersion programs, workshops, storytelling circles, and cultural camps. Chief and Council also identifies a Youth portfolio under Councillor Wade Baxter.",
