    "contact": "Band Office\n\nEmail: reception@flyingpost.ca\nTel: (807) 887-3071\nToll free: 1-800-987-3708\nFax: (807) 887-1138\n\nContact Page",
    "physical": "Physical health programming is limited in the public Flying Post, providing Healthy Babies Healthy Children, which supports pregnant women, parents, and families with children ages 0–6. The program provides information and education on healthy pregnancy, birth, baby care, pregnancy stages, home visits before and after birth, follow-up after hospital discharge, early-years child-development guidance, and referrals to other programs/services. This helps fill gaps in prenatal support, early childhood health, parenting support, healthy child development, and family connection to services",
    "mental": "Broader mental wellness support can be provided through the Family Well Being Program, which focuses on improving community health and wellbeing, empowering families to build healthy relationships, reducing family violence, reducing youth involvement in the justice system, and reducing the number of children in care. The program may include counselling, family circles, child/youth support groups, referrals, problematic alcohol and substance-use prevention/intervention, school programs, community feasts, language revitalization, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "spiritual": "Broader cultural and land-based support can be provided through the Family Well Being Program, which may include activities that revitalize Native language, community feasts, family circles, school programs, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through Flying Post First Nation’s Family Well Being Program, which is listed as supporting community wellbeing and healthy family relationships. The listed program activities include family circles, counselling, child/youth support groups, referrals to other programs and services, school programs, community feasts, problematic alcohol and substance-use prevention/intervention, language revitalization activities, and traditional land-based healing events. These supports help address family stress, emotional wellbeing, family violence prevention, child/youth wellbeing, and culturally grounded healing.",
    "survivors": "Broader support can be provided through the Family Well Being Program, which may include counselling, family circles, referrals, community feasts, Native-language revitalization, problematic alcohol and substance-use prevention/intervention, and traditional land-based healing events",
    "youth": "Youth and children are supported through Flying Post’s Healthy Babies Healthy Children and Family Well Being Program. Healthy Babies Healthy Children supports parents and children under age 6 through pregnancy and baby-care education, home visits, early-years development guidance, and referrals. The Family Well Being Program may include child/youth support groups, school programs, counselling, referrals, language revitalization activities, community feasts, and traditional land-based healing events. These supports help children, youth, and families through early childhood development, family wellbeing, cultural connection, school-based support, and prevention-focused programming.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through the Family Well Being Program, which may include family circles, child/youth support groups, school programs, community feasts, Native-language revitalization activities, and traditional land-based healing events. These activities provide possible community-based pathways for connecting youth with Elders/knowledge holders around language, culture, family wellbeing, and land-based healing,",
