    "contact": "Main Office\nPhone: 807-469-5191\nFax 807-469-1315\nEmail: northcariboulakefirstnation@knet.ca\n\nContact",
    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through Sena Memorial Nursing Station and related programs, including physician visits from Sioux Lookout, health awareness/counselling, prevention workshops, diabetes, immunization, sexual health and communicable-disease clinics, palliative care when required, prenatal coordination, home visits for the sick, elderly, new mothers and people with health-care needs, medical travel coordination, and Ontario Telemedicine Network access to specialist care.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through the Mental Health Program at Sena Memorial Nursing Station, which supports members affected by mental health and addictions issues. Services include counselling, cultural activities, feasts and ceremonies, group workshops, wellness education, fitness activities, referrals to psychologists, psychiatrists, counselling, treatment centres, and aftercare coordination, with focus areas including addictions, depression, family violence, health promotion, and stress management",
    "spiritual": "Broader cultural/spiritual support is listed through the Mental Health Program and Family Well Being Program, including cultural activities, feasts and ceremonies, Native-language revitalization, family circles, school programs, community feasts, and traditional land-based healing events. This should be recorded as broader cultural/spiritual wellness support,",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through the Mental Health Program, Family Well Being Program, Health Services, NNADAP/Suboxone-related supports, and prevention programming. Listed supports include counselling, group workshops, wellness education, referrals, aftercare coordination, family circles, child/youth support groups, alcohol/drug-abuse prevention and intervention, school programs, community feasts, Native-language revitalization, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "survivors": "Broader Elder and wellness support can be provided through Health Services, Mental Health Program, Family Well Being Program, Home and Community Care, and the listed Falls Prevention and Community Elder Exercise Program; supports include home visits for elderly members, counselling, cultural activities, feasts/ceremonies, family circles, referrals, Native-language revitalization, and traditional land-based healing events",
    "youth": "Youth and children are supported through Early Childhood Development, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, Maternal Child Health, Native Sena School, Family Well Being Program, Mental Health Program, and community education supports. Services include parenting support, healthy pregnancy/baby-care education, home visits, child development guidance, school readiness, nutritious snacks, indoor/outdoor play, Oji-Cree language, JK–Grade 8 schooling, special education, breakfast program, library/gym access, cultural/traditional outings such as fishing and trapping, summer school/camps, counselling, child/youth support groups, and land-based healing events.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through the Family Well Being Program, Mental Health Program, Early Childhood Development, and Native Sena School, where listed activities include family circles, child/youth support groups, Native-language revitalization, community feasts, traditional land-based healing events, cultural activities, feasts/ceremonies, Elder/community involvement in early childhood programming, Oji-Cree language learning, and cultural outings such as fishing and trapping",
