    "contact": "Main Contacts\nBand Office Phone: (807) 773-5578\nCrisis: 807-773-5007 - On-Reserve Police\nAmbulance Emergency1-877-351-2345\nFax: (807) 773-5536\nAfter Hours Phone: 1-888-310-1122\nMailing Address: PO Box 323, Pikangikum, ON P0V 2L0 \n\nEenchokay Birchstick School\nPhone: 807-773-5561",
    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through Pikangikum Health Authority services, including Nursing Station, physician services, X-ray, lab, ultrasound, pharmacy, emergency medical services, immunization and communicable disease services, dental services, medical transportation, telemedicine, chronic care, palliative care, Home & Community Care, diabetes programming, and home hemodialysis in progress. These services support emergency care, primary care, diagnostics, prevention, chronic disease care, medical travel, and home-based care.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through Pikangikum Health Authority’s mental wellness services, including Choose Life & Land-Based Healing, Youth Hub activities and programs, Mental Health & Addictions, Crisis Intervention, Family Wellbeing, and wellness supports for youth, adults, Elders, infants and children. The nursing page also lists mental health support, addictions, and land-based healing as part of the health team’s role in the community.",
    "spiritual": "Broader cultural/spiritual support can be provided through Choose Life & Land-Based Healing, Family Wellbeing, Elders Complex / Knowledge Keepers in Continuing Care, and land-based healing connected to mental wellness programming. These should be recorded as broader cultural, land-based, and knowledge-keeper supports",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through Pikangikum Health Authority’s Crisis Intervention, Mental Health & Addictions, Choose Life & Land-Based Healing, Youth Hub activities and programs, Family Wellbeing, Hotel/Safe House, and continuing-care supports. These services help address crisis needs, addictions, youth wellness, family wellbeing, land-based healing, safety/support needs, and emotional wellness across age groups.",
    "survivors": "Broader Elder and healing support can be provided through Elders services, Elders Complex / Knowledge Keepers in Continuing Care, Home & Community Care, Chronic Care, Palliative Care, Mental Health & Addictions, Crisis Intervention, Family Wellbeing, and Choose Life & Land-Based Healing",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Pikangikum Health Authority wellness services and Pikangikum Education Authority. Health-related youth supports include Choose Life & Land-Based Healing, Youth Hub activities, Mental Health & Addictions, Crisis Intervention, Early Years screening/developmental services, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, FASD services, Family Wellbeing, dental, medical transportation, and Home & Community Care. Education supports include Eenchokay Birchstick School for JK–Grade 12, school bus transportation, Wahsa Distance Education for Grades 9–12, and post-secondary financial assistance plus academic/social counselling support through NNEC.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through Choose Life & Land-Based Healing, Youth Hub activities, Family Wellbeing, Elders Complex / Knowledge Keepers in Continuing Care, Home & Community Care, and community wellness services, creating possible pathways for youth to connect with Elders/knowledge holders through land-based healing, family wellbeing, continuing care, and knowledge-keeper involvement.",
