    "contact": "Band Office\nPhone: 807-595-2527\nFax: 807-595-1119\n\nChief\nRobert Alexander Beardy\nEmail: Robertbeardy@sachigo.ca",
    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through the Isaac Barkman Memorial Nursing Station / Health Centre, which offers nursing-station care, visiting physician consultations, diabetes/immunization/sexual health/communicable-disease clinics, palliative care when needed, prenatal coordination, home visits for the sick, elderly, new mothers and people with health-care needs, medical appointment travel coordination, OTN specialist access, health education/prevention workshops, emergency-response education, and medication/appointment support.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is provided through the Health Centre, Mental Health Program, Crisis Intervention, NNADAP, and Family Well Being Program. Supports include health counselling, mental-health awareness, depression/family-violence/stress-management information, crisis support for family violence and suicide, addiction support, AA/NA meetings when required, prevention education, cultural/spiritual gatherings, individual/group discussions, sharing circles, support groups, referrals, aftercare, home visits, and phone follow-up.",
    "spiritual": "Broader cultural/spiritual support can be provided through NNADAP and Family Well Being programming, including cultural and spiritual events, cultural and spiritual gatherings, community feasts, family circles, school programs, Native-language/cultural supports, and traditional land-based healing events. Regular church services are also listed through Pentecostal, Anglican, and Full Gospel assemblies.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through the Mental Health Program, Crisis Intervention, NNADAP, Family Well Being Program, and Health Centre. Supports include counselling, crisis response for family violence and suicide, safety support, family meetings for crisis resolution, sharing circles, support groups, family circles, child/youth support groups, referrals, aftercare, home visits, prevention education, community feasts, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "survivors": "Broader Elder and wellness support can be provided through the Health Centre, Family Well Being Program, NNADAP, Crisis Intervention, and community cultural/spiritual supports, including home visits for elderly members, counselling, sharing circles, family circles, referrals, community feasts, cultural/spiritual gatherings, and traditional land-based healing events",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Martin McKay Memorial School, Education Department, Junior Canadian Rangers, Family Well Being Program, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, Mental Health Program, NNADAP, and community recreation. Supports include JK–Grade 8 schooling, special education, post-secondary financial/academic/social counselling support, KiHS distance education, youth ages 12–18 learning first aid, hunting/fishing, Native customs/traditions, healthy living, staying in school and drug/alcohol awareness, child/youth support groups, school programs, healthy child development, and community events.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through Family Well Being, NNADAP, Junior Canadian Rangers, school/community programming, church services, community hunts and feasts, jamborees, sports tournaments, ice fishing derby, cultural/spiritual gatherings, school programs, Native customs/traditions learning, sharing circles, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "population": "985.0",
