        "item": "How are youth supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nMartin McKay Memorial School: Provides JK-8 education with modern tech (iPads, VR) and Oji-Cree language instruction.\n Sachigo Lake First Nation - Martin McKay Memorial School - Library Services - northwesthealthline.ca \n\nSport and recreation programs in Indigenous communities | ontario.ca\n\nRevised information:\nYouth are supported through Martin McKay Memorial School, Education Department, Junior Canadian Rangers, Family Well Being Program, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, Mental Health Program, NNADAP, and community recreation. Supports include JK–Grade 8 schooling, special education, post-secondary financial/academic/social counselling support, KiHS distance education, youth ages 12–18 learning first aid, hunting/fishing, Native customs/traditions, healthy living, staying in school and drug/alcohol awareness, child/youth support groups, school programs, healthy child development, and community events.",
