    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through Shoal Lake 40 Health Services and its medical building, where licensed medical professionals visit on regular rotations. Supports include medical referrals, appointment help, out-of-community transportation/hotel coordination, Baby Hampers, Nutrition Bingo, Community Kitchens, Healthy Living activities, clinic days with WNHAC Nurse Practitioner, WNHAC Community Clinic Nurse, WNHAC Diabetes Education Nurse/Dietician, KCA Primary Care Nurse, KCA Doctor, and KCA Home Care Nurse, plus Medical Driver support.",
    "mental": "Health, Social Services, Culture, and Recreation show broader wellbeing supports through health services, social gatherings, cultural events, ceremony/teachings, and sport/recreation. 211 adds community-listed supports through Aboriginal Healing and Wellness, Family Well Being, Jordan’s Principle, and NNADAP, including peer counselling, talking circles, family violence prevention, referrals, child/youth support groups, addiction services, mental health services, Elder services, traditional healing, and land-based healing events.",
    "spiritual": "Broader spiritual/cultural support is shown through the Culture page, which says Shoal Lake 40 brings the community together through ceremony, teachings and cultural events, including powwows, medicine gathering, ribbon skirt making, and beading; also  traditional gatherings, traditional teachings, feasts, traditional healing services, Elder services, Native-language revitalization, and traditional land-based healing through Shoal Lake 40 services.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through Health, Social Services, Culture, and Recreation pathways, including health-service access, social events/gatherings, ceremony, teachings, cultural events, and recreation opportunities for youth and community members. Shoal Lake 40-listed supports such as Aboriginal Healing and Wellness, Family Well Being, Jordan’s Principle, and NNADAP, including peer counselling, talking circles, advocacy, referrals, family circles, child/youth support groups, family violence prevention, addiction supports, traditional teachings, feasts, and land-based healing events.",
    "survivors": "Broader Elder/healing support can be provided through Shoal Lake 40’s health, culture, social, and recreation pathways, including medical support, ceremony, teachings, cultural events, social gatherings, and recreation; also peer counselling, talking circles, traditional gatherings, traditional teachings, feasts, family circles, referrals, Elder services, traditional healing, Native-language revitalization, and land-based healing events,",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through official recreation, social, culture, health, and education-related pathways. Recreation offers sport and recreation opportunities for youth/community members, including Flyers team, volleyball tournaments, walkathons, hikes, and active-youth events; the Culture page lists ceremony, teachings, powwows, medicine gathering, ribbon skirt making, and beading. Harvey Redsky Memorial School for JK–Grade 8, Native language, breakfast program, bus transportation, cultural outings such as ice fishing, dog sledding and snowshoeing, plus Jordan’s Principle, Family Well Being, child/youth support groups, school programs, and education/post-secondary supports.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through official culture, recreation, social, health, and education pathways, including ceremony, teachings, powwows, medicine gathering, ribbon skirt making, beading, social gatherings, sports/recreation, walkathons, hikes, and school/community activities; Talking circles, traditional gatherings/teachings, feasts, Elder services, Native-language revitalization, child/youth support groups, cultural outings, and traditional land-based healing events as possible community-based ways to connect youth with Elders/knowledge holders.",
