    "link": "Webequie First Nation",
    "contact": "Lorraine Whitehead - Chief\nEmail: lorrainewh@webequie.ca\nCell Phone: (807) 629-9589\n\nCornelius Wabasse - Deputy Chief\nEmail: cornelw@webequie.ca\nCell Phone: (807) 620-7170\n\nEric Shewaybick - Councillor\nEmail: erics@webequie.ca\nCell Phone: (807) 633-4580\n\nDorothy Wabasse - Band Administrator Assistant\nEmail: dorothyw@webequie.ca\nPhone: (807) 353-6531 | EXT 230\n\nContact Information",
    "physical": "Physical health support is provided through Webequie’s Nursing Station and health programs. The Nursing Station houses mental-health workers and, through directory details, is listed as coordinating care with community health nurses/nurse practitioners, a community health representative, full-time counsellors, visiting physicians twice per month, diabetes, immunization, sexual health and communicable-disease clinics, dental/optometry visits, prenatal coordination, home visits for the sick, elderly, new mothers and people with health-care needs, medical travel support, and OTN specialist access.",
    "mental": "Mental health support is through Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win, which provides education, awareness, training, workshops, and sharing/talking circles on issues including health and wellness and mental health. Nursing Station also says the Nursing Station houses mental-health workers; directory sources add counselling, wellness activities, crisis intervention, NNADAP, Family Well Being, and a Mental Health Program through the Nursing Station.",
    "spiritual": "Broader cultural/spiritual support can be reflected through Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win sharing/talking circles and the Future page, which says respected Elders pass knowledge and wisdom to youth; Family Well Being activities such as Native-language revitalization, community feasts, family circles, school programs, and traditional land-based healing events.",
    "emotional": "Emotional support can be provided through Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win, Nursing Station mental-health workers, and approved directory-listed supports. Services include education/awareness, workshops, sharing/talking circles, counselling, wellness activities, health counselling, referrals, Family Well Being activities, crisis intervention for family violence and suicide, safety support, crisis planning, debriefing, stabilization, advocacy, and referrals.",
    "survivors": "Broader Elder/healing support can be provided through official Elder-youth knowledge sharing, Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win sharing/talking circles, Nursing Station mental-health workers, Health Services, Family Well Being, and Crisis Intervention, including counselling, referrals, advocacy, community feasts, Native-language revitalization, crisis support, and land-based healing",
    "youth": "Youth are supported through Elder-youth knowledge sharing, Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win, Nursing Station wellness supports, Family Well Being, Healthy Babies Healthy Children, Mental Health Program, First Nation School, and Webequie Education Authority. Supports include education/awareness, workshops, sharing/talking circles, child/youth support groups, school programs, wellness activities, cultural activities/crafts, Native-language revitalization, community feasts, traditional land-based healing events, and health supports through the Nursing Station.",
    "connect": "Broader connection can be supported through Webequie’s Elder-youth knowledge-sharing pathway, Web Equay Mamow-No-Kii-Win sharing/talking circles, Family Well Being, school programs, Native-language revitalization, community feasts, cultural activities/crafts, wellness activities, and traditional land-based healing events; these create community-based spaces for youth to connect with Elders/knowledge holders",
