        "communityKey": "whitefishriverfn",
        "item": "How can we connect survivors and youth?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nBuild on Existing Resources such as WRFN Health & Social Services by collaborating with them for programs on suicide prevention, food security, and recreation that can involve all ages\nHealth & Social Services - Whitefish River First Nation\n\nRevised information:\nBroader connection can be supported through the Seven Fires Youth & Elders Centre, Education programming based on the Seven Grandfather Teachings and Medicine Wheel, Youth Program activities, community events, recreational activities, traditional knowledge keepers/healers, Elder in Residence, and youth/elder centre activities such as social, recreational, therapeutic, craft, exercise, Lunch & Learn, and youth events.",
        "date": "2026-06-08 11:56:29.880000",
        "note": "",
        "links": [
          "https://www.whitefishriver.ca/health-social-services"
        ]
