      {
        "kind": "correction",
        "community": "MAAMWESYING",
        "communityKey": "maamwesying",
        "item": "Mental Health Programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nwholistic health and well being\n\nRevised information:\nMaamwesying provides mental health and addictions support through Mental Wellness Services, Crisis Counselling, Ontario Structured Psychotherapy, Minobimaadizing Addiction Services, FASD Sabkeshiinh Ngwaagan Program, Naandwe Noojimowin, Traditional Health, and HART Hub-related roles listed through Maamwesying postings, including Mental Wellness Counsellors, Residential Support Workers, Peer Support Workers, and Nurse Practitioner – Virtual Mental Health & Addictions. Mental Wellness Services assist men and women 18+ in maintaining wholistic health and well-being through traditional and contemporary mental health counselling and treatment services, including individual client-centred counselling, family and group therapy, and educational workshops. Minobimaadizing offers walk-in and scheduled treatment through a network of access points along the North Shore for outpatient services in addiction treatment and recovery, including Medication Assisted Therapy and treatment for other substance use disorders. These supports help fill gaps in counselling access, crisis support, family/group therapy, addiction treatment and recovery, outpatient access, referrals, FASD navigation, culturally safe care, and traditional/contemporary healing.",
        "date": "2026-06-09 10:13:56.892000",
        "note": "",
        "links": [
          "https://maamwesying.ca/mental-wellness-services/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "correction",
        "community": "MAAMWESYING",
        "communityKey": "maamwesying",
        "item": "Spiritual support programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nOCAN (Ontario Common Assessment of Need) \n\nRevised information:\nMaamwesying supports spiritual wellness through Traditional Health and HART Hub-related culturally grounded care. Traditional Health is rooted in the Anishnaabek worldview of harmony and balance in the physical, mental, spiritual, and emotional aspects of well-being, and Maamwesying says its goal is to facilitate access to diverse traditional healing services and cultural ceremonies and actively advance cultural safety in primary health care. The HART Hub adds related culturally grounded support by bringing comprehensive care directly to Indigenous communities and coordinating support through a no door is the wrong door approach. These supports help fill gaps in traditional healing, cultural ceremonies, spiritual wellness, cultural safety, and access to culturally grounded care.",
        "date": "2026-06-09 10:13:57.215000",
        "note": "",
        "links": [
          "https://maamwesying.ca/traditional-health/"
        ]
      }
