    "name": "ANCFSAO - ASSOCIATION OF NATIVE CHILD AND FAMILY SERVICE AGENCIES OF ONTARIO",
    "section": "Indigenous Organizations",
    "link": "https://ancfsao.ca/",
    "contact": "PUBLIC CONTACT FORM:\nThe website has a contact form to reach ANCFSAO (no general email/phone is published on the contact page itself).\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/home/contact/",
    "physical": "INDIGENOUS CARE GIVER SELECTION:\nUses the Helping Establish Able Resource-Homes Together (HEART) assessment approach to screen, engage, and prepare safe physical resource environments for Indigenous youth.\n\nINDIGENOUS FAMILY DEVELOPMENT ASSESSMENT (IFDA):\nDeploys a specialized alternative tool to standard SAFE testing to evaluate the stability, safety, and physical living conditions of candidate kinship and foster family homes.\n\nCULTURALLY CORRECTIVE SYSTEM TRAINING:\nFeatures the Strong Parent Indigenous Relationships Information Training (SPIRIT) program to build critical physical care competencies and traditional child-rearing practices for helpers across child welfare agencies.\n\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/home/about-2/training/heart-and-spirit-training/",
    "mental": "MULTIGENERATIONAL TRAUMA EDUCATION:\nProvides an immersive training curriculum designed to foster a deep, structural understanding of how historical and systemic events cause deep multigenerational trauma within Indigenous family systems.\n\nHEART & SPIRIT ENGAGEMENT:\nDeploys a holistic, identity-grounded engagement model rooted firmly in traditional Indigenous family and clan life philosophies to help potential caregivers heal modern disruptions in caring traditions.\n\nCULTURALLY FLEXIBLE WELLNESS CONTEXTS:\nAdapts therapeutic training delivery to account for diverse cultural contexts, creating a psychologically safe, responsive space that honors the distinct emotional and spiritual healing needs of individual communities.\n\nONLINE RESOURCES FOR MENTAL WELLNESS & SOCIAL CONNECTION:\nMember-only resources (restricted to site members).\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/portfolio/online-resources-for-mental-wellness-and-social-connection/",
    "spiritual": "CULTURAL RESOURCES FOR FAMILIES:\nCulturally-based resources grounded in traditional teachings.\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/programs-and-resources/cultural-resources-for-families/",
    "emotional": "MEMBER-ONLY WELLNESS RESOURCES:\nOnline Resources for Mental Wellness & Social Connection (restricted to site members).\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/portfolio/online-resources-for-mental-wellness-and-social-connection/",
    "survivors": "Direct Commitment Statements: Although the main /home/resources/ page contains restricted content for members, the related blog updates and announcements tied directly to this section (such as their National Day for Truth & Reconciliation updates) explicitly state that ANCFSAO stands to honor children taken by the Residential School System and acknowledge its \"legacy of historic harms.\"\n\nFocus on Overrepresentation: In these same resources and updates, they explicitly reinforce their \"commitment to working with our member agencies, their First Nations and sector stakeholders to reduce the overrepresentation of Indigenous children in care.\"\n\nEvidence-Based Advocacy: The resources menu hosts the FNOIS Report (First Nations Ontario Incidence Study of Reported Child Abuse and Neglect), which is a key tool they use for sector advocacy to analyze, address, and reshape child welfare data regarding Indigenous children.Link:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/home/resources/",
    "youth": "YOUTH IN TRANSITION RESOURCE GUIDE (2022):\nGuide supporting youth leaving care (Housing, Education, Employment, Health & Wellness, Finances, Identification).\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/ANCFSAO-Resource-Guide_Youth-in-Transition_2022.pdf",
