        "item": "How are youth supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nYouth are supported through Resources for Youth and the Youth in Transition: Pathways to Independence resource guide (2022), covering six areas - Housing, Education, Employment, Health & Wellness, Finances, and Identification; the Post-Majority Care Services (PMC) Toolkit (developed with First Nations, agencies and Indigenous Services Canada) for wrap-around supports past the age of majority; the Indigenous Youth Advisory Council (IYAC, est. Jan 2023); and partnership with the Ontario Justice Education Network (OJEN) on housing and discrimination barriers.\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/ANCFSAO-Resource-Guide_Youth-in-Transition_2022.pdf\n\nRevised information:\nYOUTH IN TRANSITION RESOURCE GUIDE (2022):\nGuide supporting youth leaving care (Housing, Education, Employment, Health & Wellness, Finances, Identification).\nLink:\nhttps://ancfsao.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/ANCFSAO-Resource-Guide_Youth-in-Transition_2022.pdf",
        "date": "2026-06-10 11:01:16.152000",
