        "item": "Emotional support programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nFamily Well-Being Program (integrated preventative care); Behavioural Therapy Model Program (self-regulation, self-esteem, coping for children/youth); Prevention and Support Services; Triple P (Positive Parenting Program); Jordan's Principle advocacy.\nLink:\nhttps://www.nog.ca/services/family-well-being\n\nRevised information:\n\nFAMILY WELL-BEING\nFamily Well-Being is an intensive early intervention program focused on providing support to families to minimize identified risk of involvement in Child Welfare, deescalating protection concerns, and supporting the reunification of families with children in out of home placements\nLink:\nhttps://www.nog.ca/services/family-well-being",
