      {
        "kind": "correction",
        "community": "Ontario Aboringinal Housing",
        "communityKey": "ontarioaboringinalhousing",
        "item": "Column Q",
        "description": "Previous information:\nProvincial scope: serves off-reserve First Nation, Inuit and Métis people across urban and rural Ontario (not a fixed member-community list); manages 3,000+ housing units and serves 12,400+ people daily through regional offices in Sault Ste. Marie, Dryden, Peterborough, Hamilton and London. Board Director-Member organizations: OFIFC, ONWA, and the Métis Nation of Ontario.\n[Proof of 12,400 people/day: https://www.housingpartnership.ca/ontario-aboriginal-housing-services]\nLink:\nhttps://www.ontarioaboriginalhousing.ca/about\n\nRevised information:\nDIRECTOR MEMBER ORGANIZATIONS:\nGoverned and supported by a unified board representing three of the largest off-reserve Indigenous organizations in the province:\n* Ontario Federation of Indigenous Friendship Centres (OFIFC)\n* Ontario Native Women's Association (ONWA)\n* Métis Nation of Ontario (MNO)\n\nRURAL & URBAN HOUSING FOOTPRINT:\nProvides safe, affordable, and rent-geared-to-income housing solutions to self-identifying First Nations, Métis, and Inuit individuals, as well as non-Indigenous people, across various municipal sectors of Ontario (including featured housing locations like Cache Bay, Hanmer, and Cochrane).\n\nREGIONAL MANAGEMENT NETWORKS:\nCoordinates distinct regional housing, program, and maintenance systems through active partner branches, including the Mocreebec Housing Association, Infinity Property Services (Thunder Bay and Barrie), and dedicated OAHS Property Management operations across Dryden, Sault Ste. Marie, Peterborough, Hamilton, and London.\nLink:\nhttps://www.ontarioaboriginalhousing.ca/rental-housing",
        "date": "2026-06-10 12:56:23.727000",
        "note": ""
      }
