        "communityKey": "northshorehealthnetwork",
        "item": "Column Q",
        "description": "Previous information:\nServes the North East Algoma catchment across three sites: Blind River, Thessalon, and Richards Landing-Matthews (St. Joseph Island), and surrounding townships. Partners with Maamwesying / North Shore First Nations and Nogdawindamin for Indigenous patient care. (Catchment area rather than a fixed member-community list.)\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/\n\nRevised information:\nREGIONAL MEDICAL SITES:\nServes multiple community regions across North East Algoma through three distinct physical healthcare operating sites:\n* Blind River (525 Causley St)\n* Thessalon\n* Richards Landing–Matthews (St. Joseph’s Island)\n\nTRADITIONAL TERRITORY FIRST NATIONS:\nProvides explicit healthcare access and services throughout the traditional territory of the Anishnaabeg peoples, directly supporting four local communities covered by the Robinson Huron Treaty of 1850:\n* Garden River First Nation\n* Thessalon First Nation\n* Mississauga First Nation\n* Serpent River First Nation\n\nTREATY BOUNDS:\nOperates medical services across geographical areas governed by historical agreements, recognizing the traditional lands of the Robinson Huron Treaty of 1850 and Treaty 11 of 1798 (spanning what is now known as St. Joseph’s Island). Link:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/",
        "date": "2026-06-10 12:37:14.787000",
