    "contact": "HEAD OFFICE:     473B HIGHWAY 17 WEST, CUTLER, ON       Phone: 705-844-2021\nFax: 705-844-2844                                               \nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/contact-us/",
    "physical": "PRIMARY HEALTH CARE\nTeam includes                                                              Physicians\nNurse Practitioners\nClient Care Coordinators\nRegistered Dietitians\nDiabetes Nurse Educators\nDental Hygienist\nHealth Promotion Educators\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/primary-health-care/\n\nMINOMODZAWIN DIABETES PROGRAMME\nMinomodzawin means 'To Live Well' - health promotion and activities for the prevention of diabetes.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/diabetes-education-program/\n\nHOME & COMMUNITY CARE\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/community-support-services/",
    "mental": "MENTAL HEALTH PROGRAMMING\n\nMENTAL WELLNESS SERVICES\nAssists adults (18+) through traditional and contemporary counselling - individual, family and group therapy.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/mental-wellness-services/",
    "spiritual": "TRADITIONAL HEALTH\nFacilitates access to diverse traditional healing services and cultural ceremonies; coordinates 1-2 Gatherings annually with Anishnaabek teachings.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/traditional-health/",
    "emotional": "MENTAL WELLNESS (OCAN + counselling)\nUses the Ontario Common Assessment of Need; general counselling for individuals, couples or groups using traditional and contemporary practices.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/mental-wellness-services/",
    "survivors": "TRADITIONAL HEALTH (residential-school focus)\nCommunities autonomously select and coordinate traditional healing and ceremonies to address the effects of residential school.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/traditional-health/",
    "youth": "The N’Mninoeyaa Aboriginal Health Access Centre and the Baawaating Family Health Clinic operate and provide services to you under the principle of the Circle of Care. The Circle of Care is a team of health care providers that will need access to your health information in order to work closely with you to make decisions regarding your health care plan.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/circle-of-care/",
    "connect": "TRADITIONAL GATHERINGS\nAHAC coordinates 1-2 regional Gatherings annually, rotated across the region to increase accessibility for all community members.\nLink:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/traditional-health/",
