        "community": "North Shore Health Network",
        "communityKey": "northshorehealthnetwork",
        "item": "How are survivors supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\n24/7 Emergency Departments as the first point of safety and stabilization; Social Work team for on-site safety planning before discharge; Victim Services. Hub-and-spoke referrals to the Counselling Centre of East Algoma for violence-against-women and sexual-assault support (NSHN has no internal shelter/SATC).\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/victimservices\n\nRevised information:\n24/7 EMERGENCY ENTRY & SOCIAL WORK\nERs are the entry point for safety; Social Work provides on-site safety planning.\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/about-5-1\n\nVICTIM SERVICES\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/victimservices",
