        "description": "Previous information:\nResearch Link Resources:\nPrograms and Services - Indigenous Friendship Centre of Sault Ste Marie \n\nIndigenous Friendship Centre in Sault Ste Marie (The) - Family Support Program\n\n\nEducation & Employment: Homework help, tutoring, and the Kina Awiiya Secondary Program (16+) for school retention and career training.\n\nCultural Connection: Traditional dancing, singing, drumming, and craft sessions.\n\nHealth & Wellness: Individual/peer counseling, mental health services, and anti-substance abuse education.\n\nJustice Support: The Indigenous Courtwork Program offers advocacy for youth involved in the justice system.\n\n\nRevised information:\nAkwe:go (Urban Aboriginal Children's Program, ages 7-12); Wasa-Nabin (Urban Indigenous Youth, ages 13-18); homework help and tutoring; Kina Awiiya Secondary Program (16+, school retention and career training); cultural activities (dancing, drumming, crafts); peer counselling; Indigenous Courtwork advocacy for youth.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services",
