        "item": "How can we connect survivors and youth?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nResearch Link resources:\nPrograms and Services - Indigenous Friendship Centre of Sault Ste Marie \nIndigenous Friendship Centre in Sault Ste Marie (The) - Family Support Program \nIndigenous Friendship Centre in Sault Ste. Marie - OFIFC\n\nThe Sault Ste. Marie Indigenous Friendship Centre (SSMIFC) connects survivors and youth through holistic, culture-based programming, including Elder teachings, sharing circles, and afterschool activities. Initiatives like the Akwego program, youth leadership initiatives, and cultural crafts create intergenerational spaces that foster healing, mentorship, and community strength\n\nRevised information:\nSurvivors and youth are brought together through culture-based programming: Elder teachings, sharing circles, afterschool activities, the Akwe:go program, youth leadership initiatives, cultural crafts, and community gatherings/events celebrating Indigenous culture - creating intergenerational spaces for healing and mentorship.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services",
