        "communityKey": "saultstemarieindigenousfriendshipcentre",
        "item": "Additional Links that may be relevant",
        "description": "Previous information:\nAdditional information:\n\nThe National Association of Friendship Centres (NAFC) acts at the federal/national level,\n\n the Ontario Federation of Indigenous Friendship Centres (OFIFC) operates at the provincial level, \n\nand individual Friendship Centres serve as local/community-level hubs. \n\nTogether, they form a \"Friendship Centre Movement\" providing, services to urban Indigenous people.\n\nRevised information:\nIFCSSM program clusters: Children & Youth (Akwe:go, Wasa-Nabin); Employment (Apatisiwin); Housing (Reaching Home, Urban Indigenous Homeward Bound); Justice (Indigenous Courtwork); Wellness (Indigenous Mental Health & Wellness, Healing & Wellness Coordinator, Life Long Care); Cultural knowledge enrichment; Family Support; N'Mninoeyaa Community Health Access Centre (376 Queen St). Latest News & events on site.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services",
