        "item": "Emotional support programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nKizhaay Anishinaabe Niin (I Am a Kind Man, men's anti-violence); Family Support Program; Apatisiwin Employment and Training Program; Indigenous Courtwork Program; Alternative Secondary School Program (Kina Awiiya Secondary, 16+); Urban Indigenous Homeward Bound. Emotional wellbeing supported across education, employment, justice and family life.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services\n\nRevised information:\nEmotional support is provided through the Akwe:Go Program, which offers intensive one-on-one support and action planning for Indigenous children and youth; the Alcohol and Drug Prevention Program, which provides holistic, culture-based one-on-one guidance for individuals and families; the Cultural Resource Program, which promotes healing, reconciliation, wellness, and support for those affected by multigenerational trauma; and the Family Support Program, which strengthens family capacity, social supports, and overall well-being through culturally appropriate services.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services",
