        "community": "Sault Ste. Marie Indigenous Friendship Centre",
        "communityKey": "saultstemarieindigenousfriendshipcentre",
        "item": "How are survivors supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nSurvivors are supported through Kizhaay Anishinaabe Niin (men), the Family Support Program, the Indigenous Courtwork Program (advocacy for those in the justice system), Reaching Home (homelessness), and culture-based one-on-one and peer counselling.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services\n\nRevised information:\nSurvivors are supported through the Cultural Resource Program, which addresses the multigenerational effects of trauma and promotes healing, reconciliation, and wellness through culturally responsive supports and access to cultural activities and teachings. Additional support is provided through the Family Support Program, which offers social supports and culturally appropriate services for children and families facing conditions of risk.                 Link:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/programs-and-services",
