        "communityKey": "saultstemarieindigenousfriendshipcentre",
        "item": "Column Q",
        "description": "Previous information:\nUrban service organization: serves the urban Indigenous population of Sault Ste. Marie and area (not a fixed member-community list). OFIFC member centre.\nLink:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/\n\nRevised information:\nSAULT STE. MARIE URBAN AREA:\nServes the urban Indigenous and non-Indigenous population living within Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario. The centre acts as a community hub welcoming all individuals regardless of race, creed, culture, status, Métis, or Inuit background.\n\nSATELLITE & PARTNER LOCATIONS:\nExtends support services across multiple dedicated community sites in Sault Ste. Marie, including Aanji Bimaadizi Homeward Bound (McNabb St.), Kina Awiiya Secondary School (Albert St. W.), Mukwa Waanzh Urban Indigenous EarlyOn, and the N’Mninoeyaa Aboriginal Health Access Centre (Queen St. E.).\n\nPROVINCIAL NETWORK FOOTPRINT:\nMaintains active membership within the Ontario Federation of Indigenous Friendship Centres (OFIFC), connecting local urban community members to a larger collective provincial network of 31 Friendship Centres across urban cities and towns.                                                                                 Link:\nhttps://ssmifc.ca/about",
