        "description": "Previous information:\nWhat is Working:        \n\nCommunity Wellness Initiatives: Provides a safe, inclusive space for Indigenous individuals to connect, offering wellness initiatives tailored to the unique needs of community members. \nLink:https://www.enjimaawinjidiyaang.com/\n\n\nYouth Mentorship & Safe Spaces: Operates dedicated safe spaces and mentorship programs specifically for youth (ages 14-24), including Wednesday Youth Drop-Ins, Youth Boys Drum Night, and a Youth Council, which foster emotional regulation and peer support. \nLink:https://www.enjimaawinjidiyaang.com/\nCultural Connection & \"Walk & Talk\": Promotes healing through ancestral wisdom and cultural connection. Programs like the \"Thursday Walk & Talk,\" \"Language Drop-in,\" and \"Craft Tuesdays\" provide low-barrier, culturally safe emotional support without the stigma of formal clinical therapy\n\nRevised information:\nCommunity Wellness Initiatives; Youth Mentorship and Safe Spaces (ages 14-24: Wednesday Youth Drop-Ins, Youth Boys Drum Night, Youth Council); Thursday Walk & Talk; Language Drop-in - culturally safe emotional support without the stigma of formal therapy.\nLink:\nhttps://www.enjimaawinjidiyaang.com/",
