        "item": "Additional Links that may be relevant",
        "description": "Previous information:\nAdditional information:\n\nThe National Association of Friendship Centres (NAFC) acts at the federal/national level,\n\n the Ontario Federation of Indigenous Friendship Centres (OFIFC) operates at the provincial level, \n\nand individual Friendship Centres serve as local/community-level hubs. \n\nTogether, they form a \"Friendship Centre Movement\" providing, services to urban Indigenous people.\n\nRevised information:\nEnji Maawinjidiyaang programs (homepage event calendar): Walk & Talk; Bowling Nights; Youth Drop-In; Learn and Lounge; Book Club; Language Drop-in; Craft Tuesdays; Youth Boys Drum Night; Youth Council; Wasa-Nabin; Alternative Secondary School; Apatisiwin. About Us: https://www.enjimaawinjidiyaang.com/aboutus. OFIFC member-centre announcement: https://anishinabeknews.ca/2023/08/01/two-new-friendship-centres-established-to-serve-urban-indigenous-communities-in-elliot-lake-and-kingston/\nLink:\nhttps://www.enjimaawinjidiyaang.com/",
