        "item": "How are youth supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nResearch link sources: \nYouth Advisory Council - Kina Gbezhgomi Child And Family Services \n\nKina Gbezhgomi Child And Family Services \n\nKina Gbezhgomi Child and Family Services - Customary Care and Foster Care \n\nYouth Advisory Council (YAC): Provides youth in care or transition a platform to influence agency service delivery and share insights.\n\nYouth In Transition Worker (YITW): Helps youth navigate services for housing, education, employment, and mental health, while teaching life skills.\n\nCultural Connection: Focuses on strengthening identity through traditional activities like regalia making, drumming circles, and Elder teachings.\n\nCommunity & Prevention Services: Offers family/support circles, social/recreational programs, and early intervention strategies.\n\nKinship Care: Prioritizes placing youth with extended family or community members to maintain cultural roots.\n\nRevised information:\nYouth Advisory Council (YAC, youth in care/transition influence service delivery); Youth in Transition Worker (housing, education, employment, mental health navigation + life skills); cultural connection (regalia making, drumming circles, Elder teachings); Kinship Care.\nLink:\nhttps://www.kgcfs.org/specialized-services/",
