        "description": "Previous information:\nYouth Advisory Council (YAC, youth in care/transition influence service delivery); Youth in Transition Worker (housing, education, employment, mental health navigation + life skills); cultural connection (regalia making, drumming circles, Elder teachings); Kinship Care.\nLink:\nhttps://www.kgcfs.org/specialized-services/\n\nRevised information:\nYOUTH-IN-TRANSITION PROGRAM:\n Serves Anishinabek youth ages 16 to 24 by providing life and social skills training, independent living support, financial literacy, education planning, and assistance finding employment.\n \n HOUSING SUPPORT PROGRAM:\n Provides culturally appropriate housing aid to youth ages 16 and 17 to help them find and sustain long-term housing, build independent living skills, and execute personal housing goals.\n \n EDUCATION LIAISON PROGRAM:\n Assists eligible youth from Junior Kindergarten up to Grade 12 with culturally responsive school system navigation, resolving learning barriers, and promoting academic achievement. Link:https://www.kgcfs.org/specialized-services/",
