        "kind": "correction",
        "community": "Indigenous Friendship Center",
        "communityKey": "indigenousfriendshipcenter",
        "item": "How are youth supported within the community?",
        "description": "Previous information:\nChildren & Youth programs: Akwe:go (Urban Aboriginal Children's Program, ages 7-12); Wasa-Nabin (Urban Indigenous Youth, ages 13-18); Youth Culture Camps; Youth Life Promotion; Urban Aboriginal Healthy Kids Program; Alternative Secondary School Program; Apatisiwin Employment and Training; Cultural Connections for Aboriginal Youth. Four OFIFC board seats are reserved for Indigenous youth (18-24).\nLink:\nhttps://ofifc.org/programs/children-youth/\n\nRevised information:\nCHILDREN AND YOUTH PROGRAMMING\nFriendship Centres provide a range of services including Children and Youth, Education, and Employment.\nLink:\nhttps://ofifc.org/programs/",
