        "communityKey": "indigenousfriendshipcenter",
        "item": "Column Q",
        "description": "Previous information:\nRepresents 29 member Friendship Centres across Ontario (provincial body). Local member centres in this scan include the Indigenous Friendship Centre in Sault Ste. Marie and Enji Maawinjidiyaang (Elliot Lake). Full member-centre directory on the OFIFC site.\n[Proof of 29 centres: https://ofifc.org/about/history/]\nLink:\nhttps://ofifc.org/friendship-centres/\n\nRevised information:\n\nPROVINCIAL URBAN FOOTPRINT:\nActs as the central governing federation representing the collective service delivery interests of member Friendship Centres across urban cities and towns throughout Ontario.\n\nPOPULATION THRESHOLD REQUIREMENT:\nMandates that new member sites must be located within an urban centre maintaining a minimum baseline population of at least 500 urban Indigenous residents.\n\nINCLUSIVE MUNICIPAL COVERAGE:\nEnforces a non-restricted service mandate to support all local urban Indigenous individuals regardless of legal status, including Status, Non-status, Métis, and Inuit community members.\nLink:\nhttps://ofifc.org/friendship-centres/",
