        "community": "Nogdawindamin Child and Family Services",
        "communityKey": "nogdawindaminchildandfamilyservices",
        "item": "Mental Health Programming",
        "description": "Previous information:\nA culturally grounded mental health program for adults and youth, focusing on \"walking the red road\" and holistic wellness.\n\n\nLink to Mental Wellness\n\n\n\nRed Path Addictions:\n\n\nSpecialized training and therapy for individuals dealing with substance use, addressing the underlying trauma.\n\n\nLink to Addictions Support\n\n\n\nChildren’s Mental Health:\n\n\nCounseling for ages 4–24, including play therapy and art therapy.\n\n\nLink to Youth MH\n\nRevised information:\nMino Madzwin (culturally grounded mental health for adults and youth, 'walking the red road'); Red Path Addictions (therapy addressing underlying trauma); Children's Mental Health (counselling for ages 4-24, play therapy, art therapy, psychiatric consultation); trauma, anxiety, depression and coping support; intake and counselling.\nLink:\nhttps://www.nog.ca/services/adult-mental-health",
