        "item": "Additional Links that may be relevant",
        "description": "Previous information:\nAdditional information:\n\nIn Canada, primary healthcare delivery and the funding of Family Health Teams  are provincial responsibilities managed by the Ontario Ministry of Health. \n\nJurisdictional Breakdown:\nProvincial Level (Primary Governance): The Wawa Family Health Team is funded and overseen by the Ontario Ministry of Health. It follows provincial best practices and is part of Ontario’s inter-disciplinary primary care model.\n\n\nRevised information:\nWFHT programs: Cardiovascular Health; Lung Health; Geriatric Support; Immunization Care; Child Wellness; Sexual & Reproductive Health; Mental Health; Nutrition Counselling (https://www.wawafamilyhealthteam.com/programs). Co-located with Lady Dunn Health Centre (www.ldhc.com); municipal health overview https://www.wawa.cc/living-here/health-care/.\nLink:\nhttps://www.wawafamilyhealthteam.com/our-team",
