        "description": "Previous information:\nAcute Care Unit (Blind River, 10 acute beds); 24/7 Emergency Departments (all three sites); Diagnostic Imaging (all sites); Laboratory Services; Physiotherapy & Rehabilitation; Geriatric Program; Community Support Services (Assisted Living, Meals on Wheels, Medical Transportation, Lifeline, Priority Assistance to Transition Home); Long-Term Care (Golden Birches Terrace). Serves a catchment of communities along the North Shore of Algoma who would otherwise travel 1-2 hours to Sault Ste. Marie.\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/blindriver\n\nRevised information:\nACUTE CARE & EMERGENCY\n24/7 Emergency Departments and acute inpatient care across the three sites.\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/emergency-department-th\nPHYSIOTHERAPY & REHABILITATION\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/physiotherapy\n\nCOMMUNITY SUPPORT SERVICES (CSS)\nAssisted Living, Meals on Wheels, medical transportation,grief support\nLink:\nhttps://www.nshn.care/css",
