        "item": "Column Q",
        "description": "Previous information:\nMaamwesying (MNSCHS) services eleven (11) First Nation communities plus the Indian Friendship Centre in Sault Ste. Marie: Atikameksheng Anishnawbek; Sagamok Anishnawbek; Serpent River First Nation; Mississauga First Nation; Thessalon First Nation; Garden River First Nation; Batchewana First Nation; Michipicoten First Nation; Chapleau Cree First Nation; Chapleau Ojibwe First Nation; Brunswick House First Nation. (Its parent body, Mamaweswen / NSTC, has 7 member First Nations: the first seven listed above.)\nLink:\nhttps://mamaweswen.com/about-mamaweswen/\n\nRevised information:\nMEMBER FIRST NATIONS:\nDelivers outreach and collaborative healthcare programs directly to eleven (11) specific First Nation communities along the North Shore:\n* Atikameksheng Anishnawbek\n* Sagamok Anishnawbek\n* Serpent River First Nation\n* Mississauga First Nation\n* Thessalon First Nation\n* Garden River First Nation\n* Batchewana First Nation\n* Michipicoten First Nation\n* Chapleau Cree First Nation\n* Chapleau Ojibwe First Nation\n* Brunswick House First Nation\n\nURBAN & OFF-RESERVE POPULATIONS:\nServes the urban Aboriginal population and off-reserve community members residing within the City of Sault Ste. Marie through the Baawaating Family Health Clinic.\n\nTRIBAL COUNCIL OVERVIEW:\nOperates under a health board made up of First Nations Chief and Council members who serve as the Executive Committee for Mamaweswen, the North Shore Tribal Council.\n\nFRIENDSHIP CENTRE PARTNERSHIPS:\nExtends therapeutic clinical coverage and primary health services to one (1) local Indian Friendship Centre within its regional footprint.                                                                       Link:\nhttps://maamwesying.ca/about-us/\n\nADDITIONAL SOURCE NAMING THE 11 COMMUNITIES:\nLink:\nhttps://thessalon.ca/news/north-shore-health-network-press-release/",
